infographic sequence-snake-steps-underline-text
data
  title The eight words, read in order, tell one story
  desc From a blank database to a correct, fast query result
  sequences
    - label Schema
      desc Declares the tables, columns, and constraints — the rules that hold the structure together
    - label Table
      desc A named grid of rows and columns, all with the same shape
    - label Rows & columns
      desc A row is one record; a column is one attribute of every record
    - label Primary key
      desc Gives each row a unique name you can point at without ambiguity
    - label Foreign key
      desc Points at another table's primary key, linking the two
    - label Index
      desc A B-tree shortcut: find rows in milliseconds instead of scanning all of them
    - label SQL query
      desc The language you send to read or change data, whatever the disk layout
    - label Transaction
      desc Wraps a multi-step change so it is all-or-nothing
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b
